<h2>Raw data</h2>
<ul class="annex-list">
  <li><a href="https://github.com/owl-fleet/labyrinthbench/tree/main/results/e1a-table1">repo <code>results/e1a-table1/</code></a> — the E1a aggregate (<code>e1a_table1.json</code>) and campaign table sources.</li>
  <li><a href="/entries/">/entries/</a> — the leaderboard entry files served by this site, one JSON per entry, CI bounds included (regenerate with <code>cli/seed_entries.py</code>).</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/assets/data/lb-e1a-raw-jsonl.zip">Raw per-run JSONL logs — E1a nav-3 campaign</a></strong> (zip, ~11 MB) — one line per run, per-turn traces included; 15 control + 13 wiped arms (9 sub-ceiling per Addendum A2, 4 ceiling per Addendum A3) with a manifest. Model-host URLs in errored-attempt records are redacted to <code>[lan-host]</code>; every other byte is as-run.</li>
  <li><strong><a href="/assets/data/lb-rev2-raw-jsonl.zip">Raw per-run JSONL logs — rev-2 look-gate campaign</a></strong> (zip, ~1.1 MB) — every arm in the <a href="https://github.com/owl-fleet/labyrinthbench/blob/main/docs/annex/look-gate-result.md">look-gate brief</a>'s tables: the three-policy observe pilot (none/recommended/forced, arm-labeled per line), the registered capped enforcement arm, the control of record, the Devstral-24B / qwen3-coder-30B / ReAct-orchestrated references, and the 120B reference (journal-verified rerun plus the superseded 2026-06-03 runs), with a manifest mapping each file to its brief cell. Model-host URLs are redacted to <code>[lan-host]</code>; every other byte is as-run.</li>
</ul>
